Bugfix: Translate the mail signature into German

The unified mail signature introduced for owncloud.online ("Best regards,",
"your %s Team", "A trademark of") had no translations, so every German mail -
password reset, share notifications, the calendar's "send link by email" -
ended in English. The three strings are now translated for de, de_DE, de_AT
and de_CH. Like the rest of each file, the signature is informal for de, de_AT
and de_CH ("Viele Grüße," / "dein %s-Team"; de_CH without ß: "Viele Grüsse,")
and formal for de_DE ("Mit freundlichen Grüßen," / "Ihr %s-Team"), so text
and signature of a mail address the recipient the same way.
A language file is only used for its exact language, there is no fallback
from de_AT or de_CH to de. Apps that include the footer with
`['app' => 'core']` already get the core translations in the language of the
mail.

The core/l10n files are maintained in this repository: the fork has no
Transifex sync. Pulling translations from the upstream project would drop
these strings again.
